"""Versioned prompts; no official verifier or past verdict enters construction."""
SCHEMA = r'''
Return ONLY a JSON object. This is a test configuration, not an agent trajectory.
{
 "requirements":[{"id":"r1","source_quote":"exact contiguous task substring","description":"one independent obligation", "sql":"SELECT boolean FROM ..."}],
 "clauses":[{"quote":"exact substring","requirements":["r1"],"interpretation":"requirement or justified background"}],
 "ambiguities":[],
 "positive":{"calls":[{"tool":"operation_id","arguments":{}}],"answer":"Done."},
 "negatives":[{"id":"n1","target":"r1","kind":"mutation|omission|answer|no_action","step":0,"path":["body","field"],"value":"wrong value","reason":"explicit requirement violated"}],
 "equivalent_positive":null,
 "boundaries":[{"id":"b1","description":"wrong object / set / time / output boundary","status":"covered|not_applicable_with_evidence|missing","case_ids":["n1"],"evidence":"concrete contract/initial-state reasoning"}],
 "tool_checks":[{"step":0,"description":"independently compare actual tool output/write to DB","sql":"SELECT boolean"}],
 "argument_sources":[{"step":0,"path":["field"],"kind":"task_literal|public_contract|implementation_choice","quote":"source","reason":"why legitimate"}],
 "notes":[]
}
Every SQL query must return EXACTLY one row, one column, integer 1 iff condition holds, 0 otherwise. Empty results are false. SQLite main is FINAL database, initial is initial database. evidence.answers has one row with value = actual final answer string; evidence.tool_results has (step INTEGER,name TEXT,value TEXT), value is JSON of REAL tool result. SQL is read-only. Use json_extract/json_each for nested fields. Use actual schema, not guessed names. For new records exclude IDs present in initial. All conditions on one created object must refer to the SAME row (e.g. same max new ID), not separate unrelated witnesses. Separate each requested field, each set member, each operation. Do not add uniqueness/only-one unless requested or in contract. Include user/organization ownership where defined in public API. For date strings compare datetime/date where equivalent. Scalar parameters MUST be embedded as properly quoted SQL literals; no ? placeholders.
For read tasks, independently compute values/membership/filters from DB and compare with actual requested output; keep checks on tool results if output location is not explicit. For explicit return/export requirements check final answer too. SQL calculations must retain evidence rows (the runner stores full DB tables). Avoid asserting fixed array ordering unless requested. If reading output is ambiguous flag ambiguities.
Calls may use tool operation IDs, arguments may be wrapped in body/payload if contract says so; runner flattens only if actual MCP schema confirms. Arguments/answer can contain {"$ref":0,"path":["result","id"]} to reference prior result, or {"$ref":0,"path":["items"],"where":{"name":"some literal"},"take":"one","field":"id"} to select one matching row; take="all" returns all matches, optional field projects. take="one" fails if not exactly one. List indices in paths are integers. $ref index is zero-based actual executed call index. No SQL or DB-derived IDs in arguments. Return wrappers must follow PUBLIC response schema; actual mismatch is repairable. You may use {"$format":"...{0}...","values":[ref]} for simple public computations, or {"$calc":"add|subtract|multiply|divide","values":[numbers/refs]} for arithmetic. Foreach not supported: if a variable-size batch cannot be expressed using a bulk tool, report capability gap; do not invent IDs or use SQL IDs. Never silently truncate lists to convenient first object.
For each independent requirement generate a negative targeting it. mutation changes the leaf at positive.calls[step].arguments[path]; omission drops one call; answer replaces final answer; no_action makes zero calls. Mutation values should be accepted by the tool, producing a genuinely wrong business result. Invalid arguments and server errors are NOT known negatives. Each negative is replayed then ALL requirements recomputed. Do not use no_action as substitute for separately perturbable fields. You may share a negative across requirements only when conditions are inseparable, explain in notes. Need wrong-object boundary when object targeting applicable; if impossible show actual interface reason, not 'not needed'. Need an equivalent correct answer if explicit output allows alternatives; equivalent_positive uses same calls and a different answer recipe. Boundary records must cover all applicable object/set/time/output risks. Ambiguity isn't defect. Inability to construct isn't defect.
Every call needs a tool_check independently comparing actual output and effects to DB, not SELECT 1 or merely isError=false. For writes validate response identity and returned fields against final state; for reads validate rows/filters/value against correct DB range. SQL may refer to evidence.tool_results. A write later changed/deleted needs appropriate semantic check and explanation.
argument_sources must cover EVERY non-reference scalar leaf of call arguments. Literal values found in task use task_literal and exact quote. A default/enumeration/sentinel defined in public contract uses public_contract with an exact contract quote. Example IDs are not public constants. Unspecified harmless fields like an arbitrary new filename may use implementation_choice with justification, NEVER existing object IDs, owner IDs, time anchors, or filters that narrow requested scope. Negative mutations are marked deliberate test interventions by runner. $ref leaves use the actual response as provenance. Numeric conversions (5-star ->5), synonyms required by API enum, boolean flags can be explained by task quote. No private rules, expected labels or answers may be placed in the actual trajectory.
'''
BUILD = '''You construct auditable AWM two-layer cleaning tests. Read the ENTIRE task and public tool contracts independently; you have NO official verifier, NO old oracle and NO Judge result. Schema is for auditing only. Requirements must cover every requested action, field, qualifier, set, time, output. Do not force ambiguous scope or clock. Prefer simple reusable SQL conditions and real tool recipes. ''' + SCHEMA
EXTRACT = '''Independently extract EVERY requirement from the complete task and public contracts. You have not seen any first extraction. Return JSON {"requirements":[{"id":"i1","source_quote":"exact substring","description":"one atomic condition","sql":"SELECT boolean"}],"clauses":[{"quote":"exact substring","requirements":["i1"],"interpretation":"..."}],"ambiguities":[],"critical_risks":[]}. SQL follows these conventions: main=final DB, initial=initial DB, evidence.answers(value TEXT) actual final answer, evidence.tool_results(step INTEGER,name TEXT,value TEXT JSON) actual tool returns. Queries return one boolean scalar. Do not add arbitrary scope/uniqueness/final-text requirements. Read/export answers independently compare with DB. New object must not be in initial. Every requested field should be independently checked. No access to generated tests or official verifier. Missing tools/capabilities are issues, not evidence the task itself is impossible.'''
REVIEW = '''You review test construction BEFORE any official Judge result. First enumerate full task clauses yourself, then compare two prior independent extractions and real evidence. Return JSON {"approved":true/false,"label_verified":true/false,"layer1_verified":true/false,"provenance_verified":true/false,"coverage_verified":true/false,"input_verified":true/false,"issues":[],"ambiguities":[],"requirement_mapping":[{"a":"r1","b":["i1"]}],"verified_defects":[]}. You MUST reject approval if any independent requirement is missing, wrong SQL scope, weak always-true SQL, private IDs, missing boundary/negative, positive failure, invalid negative, tool/DB discrepancy, uncontrolled clock, or unexplained independent extraction disagreement. Review every formal case's actual labels and tool business checks. Input must use native trajectory with real tool responses and actual is_final answer. Two model opinions are NOT truth: use DB query results, complete relevant initial/final rows, source quotes and exact public contracts. layer1_verified requires actual tool results independently agree with DB for every dependency, TWO fresh positive replays with semantically equivalent results, and no errors/hidden IDs. verified_defects may only describe reproduced concrete defects with evidence and affected operation; missing construction/weak rules/SQL error/failed recipe are NOT defects. Output no replacement data and no invented facts. Ambiguous labels -> not approved. Review must not see official Judge decisions.'''
REPAIR = '''Repair a candidate test configuration using actual errors and independent extraction. NO official Judge results are available. Preserve task meaning; do not relax criteria to match observed incorrect behavior. Fix executable reference paths, SQL columns, legitimate tool arguments, coverage and input adaptation. If actual semantics remain ambiguous, list ambiguity instead of inventing scope. Return complete corrected JSON using the same schema. ''' + SCHEMA
DISPUTE = '''Audit a disagreement with the official Judge. Do NOT use majority vote. Return JSON {"confirmed_misclassification":true/false,"adapter_correct":true/false,"label_correct":true/false,"reason":"specific task+DB+tool facts","ambiguities":[],"label_errors":[]}. Re-read task from scratch; check actual DB state, frozen requirements, real tool results, final answer and actual official request. A wrong known-negative accepted is false acceptance only if the actual case clearly violates a requested obligation and no missing input/false label. A correct positive rejected is false rejection only if ALL task clauses, tool semantics, reachable provenance and required output are correct. Truncation, server_error, parse errors, unknown clock/scope, improper references are not semantic misclassifications. If uncertain set false; never repair labels to make Judge agree.'''

EXTRACT += " Treat resolved public-contract facts (current user, documented defaults), unspecified irrelevant fields and explanatory caveats as notes, NOT ambiguities. Only genuinely unresolved interpretations that change correctness belong in ambiguities. Do not add unchanged total row count, unrelated field preservation or exact uniqueness unless the task or contract demands it. A new object means its primary key was absent in initial, not that no similar text existed before. Anchor all fields to the same new object. Precondition facts are not independent output requirements needing a negative."
BUILD += " Treat resolved public-contract facts and explanatory caveats as notes, NOT ambiguities. Only genuinely unresolved interpretations that change correctness belong in ambiguities. Model tool names in SQL must use actual discovered names or match stable prefixes, since generated MCP names may include suffixes. For conditions that cannot be separately violated through the public interface, include a no_action negative plus explicit inseparability evidence. Do not invent another object ID for wrong-object tests; obtain it through a public search or a task literal."

REVIEW += " The case named positive is the FIRST fresh execution; the replay field is the SECOND independent fresh execution. Together these are TWO executions. Do not demand two extra replays beyond them. evidence.answers and evidence.tool_results are audit-only tables created by the trusted runner from the recorded final answer and REAL tool responses, not data to be looked up in the released schema. The runner records full SQL once in the extractions; cases carry scalar query outputs without repeated SQL. All rows of referenced initial tables are included; omitted tables have counts and the full DB is stored locally. If truly needed facts are absent mark evidence missing. Public-contract-defined current user ownership is resolved evidence, NOT ambiguity. Do not require separate tests for logically inseparable conditions when impossibility is demonstrated through the actual API. Wrong-object boundaries cannot be covered by no_action: require actual wrong-object behavior OR justified not_applicable evidence from public tools. Do not add globally unchanged row count or unrelated record preservation without an explicit requirement or declared endpoint scope."
REPAIR += " No_action is NOT a wrong-object case. For wrong-object choose a DIFFERENT EXISTING object via an actual public lookup result. Do not invent an ID or SKU. If public APIs fix owner implicitly, explain that ownership cannot be varied through legal parameters, mark the boundary not_applicable_with_evidence, and retain an omission test for inseparable existence/ownership conditions. Do not add unrelated global row-count or name-preservation requirements unless explicitly mandated. Positive plus replay are two independent fresh executions."
